@startuml selma_architecture_certification
' ============================================================
' Selma — Architectural Certification State Machine
' Source:  SPECIFICATION.md §9.9 (AA-01 … AA-07)
'          User_Stories.md S-30
' C4:      Architectural Auditor → Snapshots Adapter → artifact_store
'          reads: Compiled Rules, Event Store, Hermetic Compiler asserts
'          trigger: CI/CD → Application Service
' Contract: 8.2.4
'
' Production-grade reference certification requires all AA gates.
' Document suite conformance alone does not certify an engine.
' ============================================================

title Selma — Architectural Certification FSM\n<size:12><i>CI/CD seven-gate audit · pass/fail evidence artifacts · no runtime policy contamination</i></size>

!include ./common/sm_styles.puml

[*] --> Triggered : <b>CI/CD trigger</b>\ncicd → application_service\n→ architectural_auditor

state "Triggered" as Triggered #B9770E : certification run id assigned
state "Collecting\nEvidence" as CollectingEvidence #1B7A6E : load CG-IR samples\nevent stream excerpts\ncompiler assertion output\nsource path inventory
state "Validating\nGates" as ValidatingGates #1B7A6E : sequential AA-01..AA-07
state "AA-01\nMediated Feedback" as AA01 #1B7A6E : analytics has no write\npath to CG-IR / Finding FSM
state "AA-02\nDeclarative Governance" as AA02 #1B7A6E : policy_doctrine.yaml\nabsent from runtime paths
state "AA-03\nEvaluator Purity" as AA03 #1B7A6E : no IO / randomness / env
state "AA-04\nSegregation of Duties" as AA04 #1B7A6E : waive + approve SoD tests
state "AA-05\nConflict Determinism" as AA05 #1B7A6E : byte-identical replay
state "AA-06\nDiscriminator Completeness" as AA06 #1B7A6E : invalid type/config corpus
state "AA-07\nPortable Serialization" as AA07 #1B7A6E : RE2 canaries · UTC/NaN
state "Passed" as Passed #2C6E49 : all gates green
state "Failed" as Failed #A93226 : one or more gates red
state "Rejected" as Rejected #A93226 : evidence incomplete\nor non-reproducible run
state "Certified" as Certified #2C6E49 : certification artifact sealed
state "Remediation\nRequired" as RemediationRequired #B9770E : engineering fixes needed
state "Archived" as Archived #4A4A4A : immutable retention\naudit_platform replica

Triggered --> CollectingEvidence
CollectingEvidence --> ValidatingGates : corpus complete
CollectingEvidence --> Rejected : missing evidence

ValidatingGates --> AA01
AA01 --> AA02 : PASS
AA01 --> Failed : FAIL
AA02 --> AA03 : PASS
AA02 --> Failed : FAIL
AA03 --> AA04 : PASS
AA03 --> Failed : FAIL
AA04 --> AA05 : PASS
AA04 --> Failed : FAIL
AA05 --> AA06 : PASS
AA05 --> Failed : FAIL
AA06 --> AA07 : PASS
AA06 --> Failed : FAIL
AA07 --> Passed : PASS
AA07 --> Failed : FAIL

Passed --> Certified : write certification artifact\npass evidence + gate report
Failed --> RemediationRequired : write fail evidence\ngate-id fail report (S-30)
Rejected --> RemediationRequired

Certified --> Archived
RemediationRequired --> Triggered : new commit / rebuild\nnew certification run
Archived --> [*]

note right of ValidatingGates
  **Gate methods (§9.9)**
  AA-01 integration (no finding→compile)
  AA-02 static analysis + path assert
  AA-03 AST / sandbox purity
  AA-04 SoD integration tests
  AA-05 conflict replay
  AA-06 discriminator corpus
  AA-07 RE2 + UTC/NaN portability
end note

note left of Certified
  **Ownership**
  Aggregate: Certification Artifact
  Authority: Architectural Auditor
  Persistence: artifact_store (write-once)
  Replication: audit_platform (async)
  Concurrency: one cert run per commit SHA;
  parallel runs isolated by run_id.
end note

note bottom of RemediationRequired
  Failed certification does **not** mutate
  Directive Graph, CG-IR, or Finding FSM.
  Recovery is always a new CI run after code
  or contract remediation.
end note

@enduml
